    "text": "<strong> Paragraph: </strong>\r\n\r\nThe amount of energy required to break a bond is same as the amount of energy released when the same bond is formed. In gaseous state, the energy required for homolytic cleavage of a bond is called Bond Dissociation Energy (BDE) or Bond Strength. BDE is affected by $s$-character of the bond and the stability of the radicals formed. Shorter bonds are typically stronger bonds. BDEs for some bonds are given below:\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/y1VjedD8JLq7LfjxhdWXgVlMi1sNYHZ_ikzkqGUDksQ.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/hYIQFE4CI0REUB3l90CihU9MpVVnnQf9Sf2OE7tdFC0.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/5DXHwSSjjBoyFV1aAzf3wbJw2qh5JJh-a5ug6-S5DqM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/tS7MRFgYVI0YTc78AgYQuQ3jpu90EH1gwPlmf7cNMxY.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n<br> <strong> Question: </strong>\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{CH}_{4}(\\mathrm{~g})+\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}(\\mathrm{~g}) \\stackrel{\\text { light }}{\\longrightarrow} \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{Cl}(\\mathrm{g})+\\mathrm{HCl}(\\mathrm{g})$\r\n\r\nthe correct statement is",
